{"n": 724, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "724.webp", "text": "36-6\n\n36 10300 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nFRONT OR REAR WHEEL\n\nImportant!\n\nWheel was balanced electronically —\nconform with the following procedures\nto avoid loading mistakes and\nImbalance.\n\n- Loosen wheel bolts.\n\n- Position wheel with valve facing\ndown and mount In same position.\n\n— WW several wheels have to be removed\nat the same time, mark the mounting\nposition of wheels on the tires (with\nchalk, for example).\n\n= Mark wheel to wheel hub position\n(to avold loading mistakes).\n\n= Mark wheel lock to wheel (to avold\nImbalance).\n\n—- Unscrew wheel bolts..\n\nInstailation:\n\nClean the wheel center collar and-bear-\ning surfaces of the wheel rim to remove\ndirt and old grease, and coat the center\nwith Plastilube**, before mounting a\nwheel.\n\nInspect wheel bolt threads and tapers\nfor wear, replacing the wheel bolts If\nnecessary.\n\nLubricate wheel bolt threads lightly with\ngrease, bul keep grease off of the\ntapers for Installation.\n\nimportant!\n\nWhen mounting wheels on M 3 cars It\nis necessary to consider the clearance\non the brake caliper (Incorrect wheel\ninstallation could cause damage or\ndisplacement of the pad retainers In\nthe brake calipers).\n\n** See Operating Flulds\n\nBUT\nseve\n\n|\n\nTighten the wheel bolls crosswise.\nTightening torque*.\n\nHt new wheel rims are Installed for the\nfirst time. recheck the tightening\ntorque\" after 1,000 km (600 miles).\nInstall a pertinent label to remind the\ndriver of this.\n\na) Wheel bolt - galvanized\n\nb) Wheel boll - black chrome plated\n\nc) Wheel bolt - black chrome plated\nand lockable (special equipment)", "words": [["36-6", 0.4692, 0.0311, 0.5197, 0.0536], ["36", 0.2705, 0.0734, 0.2826, 0.0853], ["10300", 0.2867, 0.0734, 0.321, 0.0853], ["REMOVING", 0.3291, 0.0721, 0.3888, 0.084], ["AND", 0.3928, 0.0721, 0.4166, 0.0827], ["INSTALLING", 0.4206, 0.0708, 0.4874, 0.084], ["FRONT", 0.3281, 0.0893, 0.3665, 0.1019], ["OR", 